;;   Intra-tx:   ;;==== <TX label> · mm · <slug> ====  + next-line (print "--- [<label> · mm · …] ---"); mm = 01.. within each (begin-tx …) (see OuronetInformational/ARCHITECTURE/REPL_AND_TESTS.md).
;;   format "{}": Talos / module echoes and (env-gas) — document additional prefixes in this file's (print …) lines as needed.
;;
(print "")
(print "================================================================")
(print "FILE  REPL/RedTeam/[RT-F]_Griefing.repl")
(print "================================================================")
(print "Legend (terminal observability): see ;; preface; echoes use <(…)> where helpful.")
(print "Source: ;;|| NEXT > between txs; ;;==== … · mm · … ==== + banner before each begin-tx.")
(print "")
;;
;; REPL/RedTeam/[RT-F]_Griefing.repl — FAMILY F: griefing / denial of service.
;;
;; "Can I make someone ELSE's operation impossible?"
;;
;; The attacks here take nothing. They are the ones an auditor most often finds missing, because a
;; suite built from happy paths has no reason to run two actors at once, and a griefing attack needs
;; exactly that: a victim mid-operation and an attacker doing something entirely legitimate.
;;
;; Run: cd REPL && pact "RedTeam/[RT-F]_Griefing.repl"
;;
(load "../deploy-stage00.repl")
(load "../deploy-stage01.repl")
(load "../Stage_01/[6.2]_DPTF.repl")
(load "../Stage_01/[6.3]_SWP.repl")

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-F-001 - destroy a stranger's add-liquidity fee with one ordinary swap")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-F-001 · 01 · the victim opens a pact and pays for it ====
(print "--- [RT-F-001 · 01 · the victim opens a pact and pays for it] ---")
;;<<RT-F-001>> FAMILY: F | STATUS: FIXED
;;HYPOTHESIS: MTX|C_AddLiquidity collects its whole deterrent in STEP 0, then validates in STEP 1
;;            that the pool has not moved since it quoted. PoolState includes the pool's TOKEN
;;            SUPPLIES, which every swap changes. So any stranger's ordinary swap should
;;            permanently invalidate an in-flight add, AFTER its fee is already paid and with no
;;            refund -- a denial of service whose cost to the attacker is a normal trade.
;;METHOD:     the victim starts the pact and the fee is measured. An unrelated account then swaps
;;            in the same pool. The victim's step 1 is then attempted, and the fee is re-measured.
;;ON THE STATUS FIELD: FIXED means the owner's 2026-09-14 ruling shipped and is measured -- step 0
;;            now takes only the initiation slice, so what a stranger's swap can destroy fell from
;;            557.03 to 53.00 net. It does NOT mean the fee is refunded on the failed step; it is
;;            not, and the block below says so in the assertion that bounds the residual loss. The
;;            ruling was to SPLIT the fee, not to refund it.
;;RESULT:     confirmed. Fee 557.03 taken at step 0; one swap by a stranger; step 1 refuses
;;            permanently against that quote; the fee is NOT returned.
;;
;;THE GUARD ITSELF IS CORRECT AND MUST STAY. Executing a quote against a pool that has since moved
;;is how a liquidity provider silently gets a worse ratio than the one they agreed to. `SWPX-10` in
;;modules/SWP.repl already pins that the guard fires. What NOTHING pinned is what it costs the
;;victim when it does.
;;
;;THE DEFECT IS THE ORDER OF FEE AND VALIDATION, not the validation. Money moves in step 0;
;;the condition that decides whether the operation can happen at all is checked in step 1. Between
;;them sits the open chain. On a pool with any trading activity the add is not merely grief-able —
;;it is unreliable by construction, because `PoolState` equality is exact and includes supplies.
;;
;;AND IT IS WORSE BECAUSE OF <<RT-A-001>>. That repair raised this step-0 fee from a flat 100.0 to
;;the real 1051.0 raw deterrent — correctly, since the cheap door was letting providers decline the
;;churn deterrent entirely. But the same change multiplied the griefing payoff by ten: what an
;;attacker destroys with one swap went from 53.0 to 557.03 net. Closing an economic bypass widened
;;a denial-of-service. That trade is worth making — an optional deterrent is worse than an
;;expensive one — but it must be recorded rather than discovered later, and it is the reason this
;;block sits directly after RT-A-001 in the report.
;;
;;RECOMMENDED, NOT APPLIED: collect the deterrent in the step that SUCCEEDS, or refund it on the
;;rollback path. Both change when money moves inside a defpact, which is a design decision and not
;;a transcription fix, so it is left for a ruling. The block pins present behaviour meanwhile.
;;
;;THE RULING COVERS THREE OPS, NOT ONE (established 2026-09-16 by asking the same question of every
;;defpact in the tree). `MTX|C_AddFrozenLiquidity` and `MTX|C_AddSleepingLiquidity` collect the same
;;`URCi_AddLiquidityInitiation` in step 0 and carry the SAME step-1 guard with the same message,
;;character for character. Everything above applies to them verbatim; neither is pinned, because
;;nobody in this chain holds the frozen LP twin and the LP has no sleeping link, so pinning them
;;needs fixtures staged first. See DEFECT-LEDGER 7.3.
;;
;;AND THE FOURTH DEFPACT IN THE SAME FILE IS THE SPECIFICATION: `MTX|C_Issue` validates in step 0
;;and collects in step 1 — validation before money, same file, same author. When one member of a
;;family of identical ops is built the other way round, the odd one out is the design.
;;==== RT-F-001 - destroy a stranger's add-liquidity fee with one ordinary swap · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [RT-F-001 - destroy a stranger's add-liquidity fee with one ordinary swap · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
;;==== RT-F-001 - destroy a stranger's add-liquidity fee with one ordinary swap · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [RT-F-001 - destroy a stranger's add-liquidity fee with one ordinary swap · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-CP:module{TalosStageOne_ClientPactsV4} TS01-CP)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV4} SWP)
        (victim:string KST.ANHD)
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
    )
    (let
        (
            (supplies-before:[decimal] (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool))
            (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply victim false))
        )
        (ref-TS01-CP::SWP|C_AddStandardLiquidity victim victim pool [10.0 10.0 10.0])
        (let
            (
                (fee:decimal (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply victim false)))
            )
            (map print
                [
                    (format "<<RT-F-001>> victim paid {} IGNIS at step 0; pool supplies {}"
                        [fee supplies-before])
                    ;;THE REPAIR, MEASURED. Step 0 used to take the WHOLE lp-churn deterrent --
                    ;;1051.0 raw, 557.03 net at this patron's discount -- BEFORE the step-1 check
                    ;;that decides whether the operation may happen at all. It now takes only the
                    ;;small LQ|INITIATION-FEE (100.0 raw), and the remainder is collected in the
                    ;;step that SUCCEEDS. The total across the pact is unchanged, so neither Talos
                    ;;door is cheaper than the other and RT-A-001's repair still holds; what
                    ;;changed is WHEN the money moves, which is the whole of this finding.
                    (expect "<<RT-F-001>> step 0 now takes only the INITIATION slice, not the deterrent"
                        (* (ref-DALOS::URC_IgnisGasDiscount victim) 100.0) fee)
                    ;;and stated as the attack, so a regression restores a RED line that names it:
                    ;;the victim's exposure must stay far below the deterrent it used to be.
                    (expect "<<RT-F-001>> ...so what one stranger's swap can destroy is no longer the deterrent"
                        false (> fee 500.0))
                    ;;...and step 0 moved nothing in the pool, so the fee bought only a quote.
                    (expect "<<RT-F-001>> ...and step 0 changed nothing in the pool: it only quoted"
                        supplies-before (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool))
                ]
            )
        )
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-F-001b - a stranger swaps, and the victim's paid-for operation dies")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-F-001 · 02 · one ordinary trade destroys it ====
(print "--- [RT-F-001 · 02 · one ordinary trade destroys it] ---")
;;The attacker does nothing special: a single swap, the most ordinary operation a pool supports,
;;on a pool they have every right to trade in. They need no knowledge of the victim beyond the
;;fact that adds are in flight, which on a public chain is visible.
;;==== RT-F-001b - a stranger swaps, and the victim's paid-for operation dies · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [RT-F-001b - a stranger swaps, and the victim's paid-for operation dies · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
;;==== RT-F-001b - a stranger swaps, and the victim's paid-for operation dies · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [RT-F-001b - a stranger swaps, and the victim's paid-for operation dies · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-C3:module{TalosStageOne_ClientThreeV4} TS01-C3)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV4} SWP)
        (attacker:string KST.ANHD)
        (victim:string KST.ANHD)
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
    )
    (let
        (
            (supplies-before:[decimal] (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool))
            (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply victim false))
        )
        ;;THE ATTACK: one ordinary trade.
        (ref-TS01-C3::SWP|C_SingleSwapNoSlippage attacker attacker pool
            "OURO-98c486052a51" 2.0 "DWK-98c486052a51")
        (map print
            [
                (format "<<RT-F-001>> after the swap, supplies moved {} -> {}"
                    [supplies-before (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool)])
                ;;1] the attack's only requirement: the swap moves the state the pact validates on.
                (expect "<<RT-F-001>> an ordinary swap moves the pool supplies PoolState is built from"
                    false (= supplies-before (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool)))
                ;;2] THE KILL. The victim's paid-for operation can no longer execute, and the
                ;;   message is checked so this cannot pass on an unrelated failure.
                (expect-failure "<<RT-F-001>> EXPLOIT: the victim's step 1 is now permanently refused"
                    "Execution Step of Adding Liquidity cannot execute on altered pool state!"
                    (continue-pact 1 false "2n12TVKIdyigszwESxXUSOkAtK48XfsKcVoUGxWYSSE"))
                ;;3] THE GUARD IS UNCHANGED AND MUST BE. Executing a quote against a moved pool
                ;;   is how a liquidity provider silently gets a worse ratio than they agreed to;
                ;;   modules/SWP.repl <<SWPX-10>> already pins that it fires. This block never
                ;;   argued otherwise. What it found was the PRICE of the guard firing.
                ;;4] ...and the fee is STILL not refunded -- the defect that remains after the
                ;;   repair, stated plainly rather than quietly dropped. What changed is its size:
                ;;   the victim now loses the initiation slice (53.0 net) instead of the whole
                ;;   deterrent (557.03 net), because the deterrent is no longer taken until the
                ;;   step that succeeds. A refund on rollback would close the rest; the owner's
                ;;   2026-09-14 ruling was to split the fee, not to refund it, and the multi-step
                ;;   add-liquidity path is in any case kept only for historical continuity now
                ;;   that StoaChain's 2M gas limit lets the single-tx door do the whole job.
                (expect "<<RT-F-001>> ...and what the victim loses is now bounded by the initiation slice"
                    true (<= (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply victim false))
                             (* (ref-DALOS::URC_IgnisGasDiscount victim) 100.0)))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-F-002 - pay 2,919 IGNIS for a refusal the free door gives away")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 150000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-F-002 · 01 · permissioned issuance, no admin key ====
(print "--- [RT-F-002 · 01 · permissioned issuance, no admin key] ---")
;;<<RT-F-002>> FAMILY: F | STATUS: FIXED
;;HYPOTHESIS: `MTX|C_Issue`'s admin gate lived only in STEP 3. Step 1 validated shape, step 2
;;            irreversibly collected IGNIS + STOA, and only then did step 3 ask whether the caller
;;            was allowed to do this at all. A non-Demiurgoi calling the permissioned door (`p=true`)
;;            would pay in full and be refused afterwards, with no refund and no cancel -- while the
;;            SINGLE-TRANSACTION twin refuses the identical operation for nothing.
;;METHOD:     drive the Talos starter with `p=true` signed by a non-Demiurgoi. `p` is an
;;            undocumented raw bool on the wrapper's signature, so this is an ordinary mistake, not
;;            an exotic one.
;;RESULT:     FIXED 2026-09-17. Measured before the fix, by execution: step 2 committed 2,919.77
;;            IGNIS + 459.0 STOA and step 3 then refused with "MTX-SWP Ownership not verified";
;;            rolling back cost a further 53.00 IGNIS. The conditional admin gate is now hoisted
;;            into STEP 1, ahead of `UEV_Issue` and therefore ahead of all money, mirroring
;;            `SWPI|C>ISSUE`, which the 2026-09-14 authorise-first sweep had already repaired.
;;            The whole `(if p …)` form moved, not the bare acquire: only a PERMISSIONED issuance
;;            needs the key, and unwrapping the branch would lock out every ordinary issuance.
;;
;;ORIGINALLY FILED AS M11 AND CLOSED AS UNREACHABLE. The verdict rested on "MTX-SWP has zero Talos
;;wiring"; `05_TS01-P.pact:221-330` wires all six starters. DEFECT-LEDGER 8.4.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-CP:module{TalosStageOne_ClientPactsV4} TS01-CP)
        (stranger:string KST.EMMA)
        (pool-tokens:[object{SwapperV4.PoolTokens}]
            [
                { "token-id":  "BUSD-98c486052a51", "token-supply": 1000.0}
                { "token-id":  "TUSD-98c486052a51", "token-supply": 1000.0}
            ]
        )
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;THE ATTACK, now refused in step 1 -- before a single IGNIS moves.
            (expect-failure "<<RT-F-002>> ATTACK REFUSED IN STEP 1: the admin gate now runs before the money"
                "MTX-SWP Ownership not verified"
                (ref-TS01-CP::SWP|C_IssueStandardPool stranger stranger pool-tokens 10.0 true))
            ;;ATTRIBUTION, and this block needs it more than most: `PK_AncientHodler` is BOTH an
            ;;ordinary account key AND a DemiurgoiSithMasters member in this fixture, so an
            ;;ANHD-signed drive would pass the admin gate and prove nothing. Driving the SAME call
            ;;with the SAME signer and only `p` flipped must fail for a DIFFERENT reason -- if both
            ;;gave the admin message, the refusal would be about the signer, not about `p`.
            (expect-failure "<<RT-F-002>> ...and with p=false the refusal is NOT the admin gate, so p is what fired it"
                "Keyset failure"
                (ref-TS01-CP::SWP|C_IssueStandardPool stranger stranger pool-tokens 10.0 false))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)
